# URL Shortener — sample requests
#   Part 1: feature 001 quickstart scenarios 1–12 (specs/001-greenfield-core/quickstart.md)
#   Part 2: feature 002 — expiry, 410 Gone, reclaim, statistics (specs/002-brownfield-analytics-expiry/quickstart.md)
#   Part 3: feature 003 — rate limiting (specs/003-reliability-abuse-protection/quickstart.md)
#
# Run with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client): click "Send Request" above
# each request, top to bottom. Later requests reuse the code returned by earlier ones.
# Start the API first:  dotnet run --project src/UrlShortener.Api --launch-profile http
# Contract (current, v0.3.0): specs/003-reliability-abuse-protection/contracts/openapi.yaml
#
# Rate limits (feature 003, per client, defaults): create 10 per minute; redirect 120 per minute
# with bursts up to 60; details + statistics 60 per minute; /health unlimited. Every request counts,
# including 400s and 404s. Beyond a budget you get 429 with Retry-After, so wait one minute between
# parts as noted below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5058

# Custom aliases are unique ignoring case, so a second run returns 409 for scenario 4.
# Change these two values (same letters, different case) or delete the dev database to re-run.
@alias = Team-Offsite-Demo
@aliasOtherCase = team-offsite-demo

# Part 2: an alias that expires one minute after creation and is then reclaimed (F2-6). Once it
# has expired it can be claimed again, so re-running Part 2 after a minute works without changes.
@seasonalAlias = Spring-Sale-Demo
@seasonalAliasOtherCase = spring-sale-demo

### 1. Create a short link (generated code) → 201, Location header, clickCount 0
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/some/long/path?x=1"
}

### 2. Follow the short link → 302 to the original URL, Cache-Control: no-store
# REST Client follows redirects by default; set "rest-client.followredirect": false to see the 302.
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{create.response.body.$.code}}

### 3. Link details → 200; clickCount includes the redirect above within about a second (clicks are stored in the background; reading details is not a click)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/{{create.response.body.$.code}}

### 4a. Custom alias → 201 with the alias as the code (case kept)
# @name createAlias
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/offsite",
  "customAlias": "{{alias}}"
}

### 4b. Aliases resolve in any letter case → 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{aliasOtherCase}}

### 5. Same alias in another letter case → 409 ProblemDetails "Alias already in use"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/other",
  "customAlias": "{{aliasOtherCase}}"
}

### 6. Unsupported scheme → 400, errors.url
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "javascript:alert(1)"
}

### 7. Missing scheme → 400 with the hint "Did you mean https://www.example.com/page?"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "www.example.com/page"
}

### 8. User info disguising the real host → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://google.com@evil.example/login"
}

### 9. Points at the shortener itself (any case/port) → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "http://LOCALHOST:5058/x"
}

### 10. Forged Host header → 201, shortUrl still on the configured base URL
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Host: evil.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/forged-host"
}

### 11. Unknown code → 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/zzzzzzz

### 12. Health (service + database) → 200 Healthy
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Extra: reserved alias → 400, errors.customAlias
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "customAlias": "API"
}

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Part 2 — feature 002: expiry, 410 Gone, reclaim, statistics
# Click counts and statistics are filled in by a background writer: allow a second after redirects.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### F2-1. (Wait one minute after Part 1: the create budget is 10 per minute.) Expiry with an offset → 201, expiresAtUtc is the same instant in UTC (2099-12-31T18:29:00Z)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/flash-sale",
  "expiresAt": "2099-12-31T23:59:00+05:30"
}

### F2-2. Expiry without a time zone → 400, errors.expiresAt "The expiry needs a time zone, ..."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/flash-sale",
  "expiresAt": "2099-12-31T23:59:00"
}

### F2-3. Expiry in the past → 400, errors.expiresAt "The expiry must be in the future."
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/flash-sale",
  "expiresAt": "2020-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### F2-4a. Alias that expires in one minute → 201
# @name seasonal
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/spring-sale",
  "customAlias": "{{seasonalAlias}}",
  "expiresAt": "{{$datetime iso8601 1 m}}"
}

### F2-4b. Before expiry → 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{seasonal.response.body.$.code}}

### F2-5a. Wait one minute, then → 410 ProblemDetails "Link expired", Cache-Control: no-store
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{seasonal.response.body.$.code}}

### F2-5b. Details of the expired link still work → 200 with expiresAtUtc and the click from F2-4b
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/{{seasonal.response.body.$.code}}

### F2-5c. Statistics of the expired link still work → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/{{seasonal.response.body.$.code}}/stats

### F2-6a. Reclaim the expired alias, in another letter case → 201; the old link and its history are deleted
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/autumn-sale",
  "customAlias": "{{seasonalAliasOtherCase}}"
}

### F2-6b. The code now redirects to the new URL → 302 to https://example.com/autumn-sale
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{seasonal.response.body.$.code}}

### F2-7a. Statistics: create a fresh link to follow with and without a referrer → 201
# @name stats
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/stats-demo"
}

### F2-7b. Follow with a referrer (send 3 times) → 302; only the host news.example is stored
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{stats.response.body.$.code}}
Referer: https://news.example/article?u=1

### F2-7c. Follow without a referrer (send 2 times) → 302; counted as (direct)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{stats.response.body.$.code}}

### F2-7d. Statistics → 200, totalClicks 5, 30 dailyClicks with today 5, topReferrers news.example 3 then (direct) 2
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/{{stats.response.body.$.code}}/stats

### F2-8. Statistics for an unknown code → 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/zzzzzzz/stats

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Part 3 — feature 003: rate limiting
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### F3-1. (Wait one minute after Part 2.) Create 11 times within a minute (send 11 times) → 429 on the 11th; the first 10 get 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/rate-limit-demo"
}

### F3-2. One more create → 429 Too many requests, Retry-After (seconds), ProblemDetails; nothing created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/links
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "url": "https://example.com/rate-limit-demo"
}

### F3-3. Other budgets are separate: following a link still works → 302
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{stats.response.body.$.code}}

### F3-4. Reading details still works → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/links/{{stats.response.body.$.code}}

### F3-5. Health is never limited (send 100 times) → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health